- How to simulate traffic split in tests and monitor drift?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to implement end-to-end tracing in a multi-tenant CNF gateway; validates generating and propagating trace context with tenant isolation using OpenTelemetry and OTLP.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry, OTLP exporter
- Trace context propagation (traceparent) and tenant tagging
- Sidecar-based instrumentation and in-cluster collector
- Validation: Jaeger/Tempo dashboards per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: derive and propagate trace context
const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
const traceId = sha256(tenant + req.path + Date.now()).slice(0, 32);
const spanId  = sha256(tenant + (req.headers['x-request-id'] || Date.now())).slice(0, 16);
req.headers['traceparent'] = `00-${traceId}-${spanId}-01`;
req.headers['X-Tenant-Id'] = tenant;
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test cross-tenant trace privacy and access controls?
- What would you monitor if downstream services drop trace headers?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design runtime policy reconfiguration with multi-tenant separation and zero-downtime updates.

## Key Concepts
- Central policy streaming via gRPC
- Per-tenant policy data model with versioning
- In-memory delta application with TTL and idempotence
- CRD design for policy declarations and rollout path

## Code Example
```proto
syntax = "proto3";
package policy;
message PolicyDelta {
  string tenant_id = 1;
  string path_hash = 2;
  uint32 rate_limit = 3;
  uint32 window_seconds = 4;
  uint32 circuit_failure_limit = 5;
  uint32 circuit_reset_seconds = 6;
  uint32 log_sample_rate = 7;
  string policy_version = 8;
}
service PolicyService {
  rpc StreamPolicy(PolicyDelta) returns (stream PolicyDelta);
}
```

